{"id":"opt-1","family":"constraint-optimization","model":"openai/gpt-4.1-nano","status":200,"ms":8028,"validJson":false,"pass":false,"text":"Let's analyze the projects to select the optimal subset that maximizes value without exceeding total cost 65, with at most two projects per group, and break ties lexicographically.\n\n### Step 1: Group projects by group\n\n**Group 0:** P00 (17,47), P04(19,47), P08(15,13), P12(15,14)  \n**Group 1:** P01(8,32), P05(22,20), P09(7,49), P13(9,40)  \n**Group 2:** P02(10,36), P06(14,37), P10(7,36), P14(5,18)  \n**Group 3:** P03(19,49), P07(18,30), P11(6,10), P15(13,5)\n\n### Step 2: Select up to two projects per group to maximize total value\n\nFor each group, select the top two projects with highest value, considering total cost constraints.\n\n#### Group 0:\n- P00 (47,17)\n- P04 (47,19)\n- P08 (13,15)\n- P12 (14,15)\n\nTop 2 based on value:\n- P00 and P04 (both 47). Total cost: 17+19=36, total value=94.\n\n#### Group 1:\n- P09 (49,7)\n- P13 (40,9)\n- P01 (32,8)\n- P05 (20,22)\n\nTop 2:\n- P09 and P13 (49+40=89). Cost: 7+9=16.\n\nRemaining options:\n- P09 and P01: 49+32=81, costs 7+8=15\n- P13 and P01: 40+32=72, costs 9+8=17\n\nChoose P09 and P13 (value 89, cost 16).\n\n#### Group 2:\n- P06 (37,14)\n- P02 (36,10)\n- P10 (36,7)\n- P14 (18,5)\n\nTop 2:\n- P06 and P02: 37+36=73, costs 14+10=24\n- Alternative: P10 and P06: 36+37=73, cost 7+14=21\n\nChoose P06 and P02 (value 73, cost 24).\n\n#### Group 3:\n- P03 (49,19)\n- P07 (30,18)\n- P11 (10,6)\n- P15 (5,13)\n\nTop 2:\n- P03 and P07: 49+30=79, cost 19+18=37\n- P03 and P11: 49+10=59, cost 19+6=25\n\nChoose P03 and P07 (value 79, cost 37).\n\n### Step 3: Aggregate selected projects and check total cost\nSelected projects:\n- Group 0: P00, P04 (total cost 36, value 94)\n- Group 1: P09, P13 (total cost 16, value 89)\n- Group 2: P06, P02 (total cost 24, value 73)\n- Group 3: P03, P07 (total cost 37, value 79)\n\nTotal cost: 36+16+24+37=113 > 65, so we need fewer projects.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Adjust selection to meet total cost <= 65\n\nOne approach: remove projects from the largest total cost groups or replace some with lower-cost alternatives.\n\nTry removing the highest-cost projects:\n\n- Remove P03 and P07 (cost 37), total now: 36+16+24=76 > 65 → still too high.\n- Remove P06 (14) from group 2: remaining group 2 projects P10 and P14:\n  - P10 (7,36), P14(5,18): total 7+5=12, total value=36+18=54\n  combined from group 2: P10 and P14 for minimal cost and high value.\n\nRecalculate total with this change:\n\n- Group 0: P00, P04: cost 36, value 94\n- Group 1: P09, P13: cost 16, value 89\n- Group 2: P10, P14: cost 12, value 54\n- Exclude group 3 projects\n\nTotal cost: 36+16+12=64 <= 65\n\nTotal value: 94+89+54=237\n\nTotal cost: 64, total value: 237.\n\nAny other combination yields lower total value or exceeds cost constraints.\n\n### Final selection:\n\nProjects: P00, P04, P09, P13, P10, P14\n\nSorted IDs: [\"P00\", \"P04\", \"P09\", \"P10\", \"P13\", \"P14\"]\n\nTotal value: 94 + 89 + 36 + 18 = 237\n\n---\n\n## Final answer:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ids\": [\"P00\", \"P04\", \"P09\", \"P10\", \"P13\", \"P14\"],\n  \"value\": 237\n}\n```","usage":{"prompt_tokens":456,"completion_tokens":1118,"total_tokens":1574,"cost":0.0004928,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.0004928,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0000456,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0004472},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}},"finish":"stop"}
