{"id":"opt-2","family":"constraint-optimization","model":"openai/gpt-4.1-nano","status":200,"ms":22020,"validJson":false,"pass":false,"text":"Let's analyze the options and constraints carefully:\n\n- Total cost must be ≤ 65.\n- At most two projects per group.\n- Maximize total value.\n- Break ties lexicographically when values are equal, based on sorted ID list.\n\n### Step 1: Determine the best combinations per group:\nGroup 0:\n- P00 (cost 17, value 34)\n- P04 (cost 13, value 43)\n- P08 (cost 5, value 35)\n- P12 (cost 18, value 20)\n\nBest two projects:\n- P04 + P00: cost 30, value 77\n- P08 + P04: cost 18, value 78 (better)\n- P08 + P00: cost 22, value 69\n- P08 + P12: cost 23, value 55\n- P00 alone: 17, 34\n- P04 alone: 13, 43\n- P08 alone: 5, 35\n\nBetween P08 + P04 (cost 18, value 78) and P04 + P00 (cost 30, value 77), P08 + P04 is better.\n\nGroup 1:\n- P01 (cost 6, value 6)\n- P09 (cost 16, value 40)\n- P13 (cost 19, value 44)\n- P05 (cost 19, value 7)\n\nTop two:\n- P13 + P09: 35, 84\n- P13 + P01: 25, 50\n- P09 + P01: 22, 46\n- P13 alone: 19, 44\n- P09 alone: 16, 40\n- P01 alone: 6, 6\n\nChoose P13 + P09 for 84 value.\n\nGroup 2:\n- P02 (cost 11, value 42)\n- P06 (cost 21, value 23)\n- P10 (cost 7, value 21)\n- P14 (cost 10, value 5)\n\nBest two:\n- P02 + P10: 18, 63\n- P02 + P06: 32, 65\n- P10 + P14: 17, 26\n- P02 alone: 11, 42\n- P06 alone: 21, 23\n- P10 alone: 7, 21\n\nChoose P02 + P06: 32, 65 (max value under cost).\n\nGroup 3:\n- P03 (cost 5, value 9)\n- P07 (cost 8, value 23)\n- P11 (cost 4, value 10)\n- P15 (cost 9, value 30)\n\nTop two:\n- P15 + P07: 17, 53\n- P15 + P11: 13, 40\n- P07 + P11: 12, 33\n- P15 alone: 9, 30\n- P07 alone: 8, 23\n- P11 alone: 4, 10\n\nChoose P15 + P07 for 53 value.\n\n### Step 2: Summing costs and values:\n- P08 + P04: 5 + 13 = 18, value: 78\n- P13 + P09: 19 + 16 = 35, value: 84\n- P02 + P06: 11 + 21 = 32, value: 65\n- P15 + P07: 9 + 8 = 17, value: 53\n\nTotal cost: 18 + 35 + 32 + 17 = 102 > 65, too high. Need to reduce total.\n\n### Step 3: Adjust for maximum total value within cost constraint.\n\nLet's consider choosing projects that provide high value but stay within 65:\n\n- Start with the top value projects:\n   - P13 + P09: value 84, cost 35\n   - P08 + P04: value 78, cost 18\n   - P15 + P07: value 53, cost 17\n   - P02 + P06: value 65, cost 32\n\nSum two key combinations to not exceed 65.\n\nCheck:\n- P13 + P09 (value 84, cost 35) + P02 + P06 (cost 32) total 67 > 65, too high.\n- P13 + P09 (84) + P15 + P07 (53), cost 35 +17= 52, total value = 137, total cost 52.\n  Total value: 84 + 53= 137, total cost: 35+17=52. All within 65.\n\nRemaining budget: 65 - 52 = 13.\n\nRemaining projects:\n- P08 (cost 5, value 35)\n- P04 (cost 13, value 43)\n- P12 (cost 18, value 20)\n- P11 (cost 4, value 10)\n- P01 (cost 6, value 6)\n- P05 (cost 19, value 7)\n- P00 (cost 17, value 34)\n- P10 (cost 7, value 21)\n- P14 (cost 10, value 5)\n\nChoose best project within remaining budget:\n- P08 (cost 5, value 35), remaining budget: 8\n- P11 (cost 4, value 10), remaining budget: 4\n- P01 (cost 6, value 6) too expensive next to P08.\n\nNow add P08 and P11:\n- Cost: 5 + 4 = 9, exceeds remaining budget of 13, but total budget is 65, total used: 35+17+5+4=61, total value: 84+44+35+10= 173.\n\nTotal cost: P13 (19) + P09 (16) + P15 (9) + P07 (8) + P08 (5) + P11 (4) = 61, total value: 84+40+53+23+35+10= 255.\n\nTotal used cost: 19+16+9+8+5+4=61, total value: 84+40+53+23+35+10= 245.\n\nRemaining budget: 4 (65-61), no better projects fit.\n\n### Final selection:\nProjects:\n- P13\n- P09\n- P15\n- P07\n- P08\n- P11\n\nSorted IDs: [\"P07\", \"P08\", \"P09\", \"P11\", \"P13\", \"P15\"]\n\nTotal value: 84 + 40 + 53 + 23 + 35 + 10 = **245**\n\nTotal cost: 8 + 16 + 9 + 4 + 19 + 9 = 65 (sum of individual project costs, matching total budget).\n\n### **Answer:**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"ids\": [\"P07\", \"P08\", \"P09\", \"P11\", \"P13\", \"P15\"],\n  \"value\": 245\n}\n```","usage":{"prompt_tokens":456,"completion_tokens":15